#
# Convention: every entry uses ${VAR:-value} so a command-line env pin still wins.
#
# D6 ROLLBACK — uncomment the next line to force the sprint-planner back onto opus
# if the codex planner lane misbehaves. Takes effect at the next launchd fire; no
# code change, no restart.
#
# MISSION_PLANNER_MODEL="${MISSION_PLANNER_MODEL:-opus}"

# DeepSeek executor lane (Mark 2026-08-06, codex-quota relief): pi + OpenRouter
# deepseek-v4-flash-0731. Gate trial: agent smoke 23/23 clean; #590 mission replay
# 12/13 held-out landed tests at $0.076 true cost / 12.6 min (plan-faithful; the
# one miss pinned a refinement beyond the plan's letter). The driver pre-probes
# pi:* pins and falls back to opus on any probe failure; the skill's Gate-3 pi
# recipe posts each run's OpenRouter spend to the $5/iteration metered ledger.
# ROLLBACK — comment the next line to return the executor to the driver default
# (codex:gpt-5.6-sol, itself probe-guarded with opus fallback).
# PRICE-PINNED 2026-08-11 (:floor = OpenRouter provider.sort=price). Bare ids let
# OpenRouter load-balance across 26 hosts, and prompt caches are PER-PROVIDER, so
# consecutive calls cached nothing. Measured: unpinned cacheRead=0 on two identical
# ~27.7k prompts; :floor cached 27,392 of 27,673 on call 2 => 4.8x cheaper per
# repeat call. Rollback: drop the ":floor" suffix (backup .bak-floorpin).
# HARD PIN REMOVED 2026-08-11 (ailang#611). This pin dated from the codex quota
# drought and made deepseek the DEFAULT — the opposite of the ratified policy
# ("codex as default, deepseek the replacement when codex is out"). The driver
# now implements the real chain: codex -> pi:deepseek(:floor) -> opus, so the
# default needs no pin here. Re-pin ONLY to force a lane for a specific fire.
# MISSION_EXECUTOR_MODEL="${MISSION_EXECUTOR_MODEL:-pi:openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731:floor}"

